  "contract": [
    "Constructor always clears the shared owner before input checks. Require nonnull config,76 bytes and exact pre_pv_v1.1.0; invalid input returns6 without allocation. No invented allocation-null guard or cleanup.",
    "Allocate212, publish owner before clearing, then reload the live owner between every immediate initializer. Preserve argument offsets, provider order, raw descriptor fields and unsigned wrapping allocation sizes.",
    "Descriptor copies76 bytes with overlap support and writes its five metadata words. Queue initializers retain16-bit field truncation while allocation uses the full32-bit shifted count, and preserve provided-buffer versus allocated-buffer index semantics.",
    "Initialize single owned record, buffer owner/64-byte buffer, descriptor pair and optional40-byte channel array. Preserve untouched reserved bytes, live count/array reads, helper return words and mode truncation.",
    "The model-owner helper overwrites the stack slots later popped into R0..R3. Its return reloads the potentially modified first parameter word after the model callback, rather than returning the incoming record address."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Direct614 paired cases execute all668 native instruction bytes and compare entire public records/allocated arena, owner writes, provider args/snapshots, helper return words, saved registers, SP, masks, guards and exact active-context FPSCR. Primitive copy/clear/string implementations execute as compiled C; allocation and four deeper ports are modeled.",
    "Four deeper ports remain unresolved: session init, short-pair init, weights getter and model creation. Replacing goodix_spo2_init with these boundaries raises application imports63 to66; boot remains22. Complete SpO2 initialization/physical operation is not claimed.",
    "The128-case lifecycle executes actual C constructor, complete existing C teardown, actual C pool initialization/allocation/free and compiled C memory functions against stock. Deep session/short-pair effects are modeled as zero and model creation returns null, so missing deep allocations are excluded. All allocations made by recovered C code are released/coalesced to the prior top.",
    "The lifecycle uses an isolated byte-fill object with exactly the same104 relocation-free machine bytes as the normal monolithic C provider. The normal build still uses its original provider object unchanged.",
    "A retained independent probe demonstrates a Unicorn2.1.4 broad write-hook discrepancy: the same ELF exits0 in QEMU and Unicorn without the hook, but1 with the no-op broad hook. Restricting the owner-write hook to its observed word preserves the original owner-write assertions and full-memory comparisons without modifying firmware. Heap tests omit the broad write trace and compare complete heap images.",
    "The model-owner return mismatch was a real reconstruction error and was corrected; callback mutation now verifies the reloaded return word. Initial QEMU startup-vector and fixture-link/setup issues were corrected before final admission. Only the final clean build and corpora are acceptance evidence.",
    "Null modeled allocation failures are logical access-shape checks, not physical MCU fault proof. Cold FP/task activation, interrupt concurrency, invalid input pointers and real allocator exhaustion/scheduler behavior remain unproven here. Caller scratch, APSR, private stack addresses and fault instruction widths excluded.",
    "No new writable state; reuse canonical SpO2 owner. All870 prior nongenerated source/object pairs, allocator and teardown objects remain unchanged; tested object equals the normal881-unit build. Source-plan/cache layout unchanged; final placement/startup still open.",
    "Final executable linking, deeper constructors/resources, other hardware dependencies, physical sensors and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware. No instruction or image identity is claimed."
  ],
